/*
 * paintedFlora.js — flora interiors painted by code (candidate, 2026-11-15)
 * =============================================================================
 * ON THE WORKBENCH ONLY. The first shaded flora (LayeredFlora.jsx) sliced the
 * OUTLINE into bands, and Kimia saw at once that it read like map contours.
 * The friends do not look like that because each began as a soft grey
 * painting that tracing then sliced into tones. So this does the same, with
 * the painting made by a script run outside the repo:
 *
 *   1. start from "lighter where the body is thick";
 *   2. disturb it with lumps, blotches and streaks at three sizes, and drag
 *      it sideways a little, so the tones stop following the edge
 *      (`veined` also adds thin wandering ridges);
 *   3. slice the result into seven tones, giving every species the SAME
 *      share of each tone, and drop any piece too small to read.
 *
 * Each entry is a species' seven layers, darkest first, each lying on top of
 * the one before. They are painted in the friends' greys #494949 … #d0d0d0
 * over a silhouette in #333333, exactly as a friend's bands are. Only flora
 * '6' and '1' are here: two shapes to judge the idea on.
 * =========================================================================== */

